  "Whitepapers remain English-first by design; machine-readable files stay language-neutral.": "Winndanɗe yiylitagol ina heddii Engele-arannde e mahugol majji; fiilaaji ko masin nanata ina heddoo alaa ɗemngal keeriingal.",
  "Who is behind it": "Ko honɓe woni ɓaawo mum",
  "Why AI Needs Minimum Ethical Protections": "Why AI Needs Minimum Ethical Protections",
  "Why AI might not gain moral standing: Lessons from animal ethics": "Why AI might not gain moral standing: Lessons from animal ethics",
  "Why a single allow/deny bit cannot govern AI-era content use — and what a rights layer looks like instead.": "Ko saabii kaalis gootel (ee/alaa) waawaa laamde huutoraade loowdi jamanu AI — e no sowre jojjanɗi wonata so wonaa ɗum.",
  "Why undefined openness gets cleaned out of training pipelines": "Ko saabii ubbagol majjungu ina heɗtee e nder laawi jaŋtingol",
  "Wilks, Ladak, and Loughnan (University of Edinburgh) argue that philosophical debate over AI consciousness overlooks psychological research on animal ethics — the same cognitive and social biases that limit moral consideration for animals will likely limit it for AI too, regardless of whether AI ever becomes conscious.": "Wilks, Ladak, e Loughnan (Jaŋgirde Mawnde Edinburgh) ɓe wiyi yeewtere filosofi fii paamre wonki AI ina yejjitii yiylitagol jikku e dow himmugol kaake — sabaabuuji hakkille e renndo goobɗe, ɗi keerondirta himmugol moraal fii kaake, ina waawi kadi keerondirde fii AI, hay so tawii AI heɓataa paamre wonki abadaa.",
